# Agent owns backend operations

The agent has shell access to the backend repo (`C:\Users\lysp\Downloads\nvccz`, port **3009**).

## Never tell the user to

- Restart the backend
- Run backend scripts, migrations, or npm commands
- Fix backend config, env, or database issues themselves
- "Try again after the server reloads"

## Always do it yourself

- Restart or kill/restart port 3009 when backend changes need to be live
- Run verification scripts, DB queries, and smoke tests against the backend
- Apply backend fixes in `nvccz` without handing off steps

If backend work is blocked (permissions, missing secrets only the user has), say what is blocked and what you need from them — not a list of commands to run.
